 ## Usage
 
+The command line interface provides four subcommands. The top‑level help shows the
+overall usage and available commands:
+
+```sh
+tally [-h] [--version] {add,list,report,export} ...
+```
+
+Each subcommand has its own options, as displayed by `python -m tally <subcommand> --help`:
+
 ```sh
-tally add 4.50 --category coffee
-tally list
-tally report
+# Record an expense (or refund) – `add`
+tally add AMOUNT CATEGORY [--note NOTE] [--date DATE]
+
+# Show the most recent entries – `list`
+tally list [--limit LIMIT]
+
+# Show totals by category – `report`
+tally report [--month MONTH]
+
+# Export all entries as CSV – `export`
+tally export [--output OUTPUT]
 ```
 
 Entries live in `~/.tallyho.json`. Set `TALLY_FILE` to use a different file.
